# Adeni agent rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for the full playbook. These rules always apply.

## Project

Trusted local services marketplace API (.NET 10, PostgreSQL, Redis, Auth0). Flutter client. Lagos / beauty vertical. SOC 2 controls from day one.

## Architecture

`Domain` → `Application` ← `Infrastructure` ← `Api`. Services return `Result<T>`. Controllers use `.Match()`. Register DI in `ServiceCollectionExtensions`.

## Security (non-negotiable)

- Tenant isolation: EF query filters + `TenantAccessMiddleware` + `X-Tenant-Id` header
- PII: use `PiiMasker`; never log full phone/email/body
- Admin `/admin/*` mutations must audit to `admin.audit_logs`
- Admin JWTs need `amr: mfa` when MFA policy enabled
- `DevBusinessAuthMiddleware` only in Development/Testing

## Current focus

Sprint 3: Auth0 + Flutter shell. See [docs/sprints.md](../../docs/sprints.md). Do not start booking unless asked.

## Workflow

Use AGENTS.md standing plays: spec → implement → debug → security audit → tests → review. Minimal diffs. Run `dotnet test Adeni.slnx -c Release` before PR.

## Tests

Integration tests: `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`, environment `Testing`, empty DB/Redis connection strings for in-memory fallback.
